# The Chrome extension is a separate workspace: its own package.json, its own
# deps (@crxjs/vite-plugin, vite), built by `bun run ext:build` from extension/.
# Vercel builds only the Next app, so the directory is dead weight there — and
# worse than dead weight, because a cold Vercel build tried to type-check
# extension/manifest.config.ts and failed on a dep that is not a root
# dependency. tsconfig.json excludes it from the build; this excludes it from
# the upload.
#
# The leading slash is load-bearing: a bare `extension` matches EVERY path
# segment of that name, which also excluded src/lib/extension/ and
# src/app/extension/ and failed the build on `Can't resolve
# '@/lib/extension/analyze'`. Anchor it to the repo root.
/extension

# .vercelignore supersedes .gitignore for deciding what gets uploaded, so
# anything that must never reach a build is listed explicitly here rather than
# inherited. Do not remove the .env lines.
node_modules
.next
.env
.env.*
.storage
